- op: discuss  # b26e
  at: '2026-09-15T21:23:15Z'  # b26e
  by: agent  # b26e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b26e
  clock: 3  # b26e
  nonce: b26e  # b26e
  message: "DONE in PR #972. An unowned marker now reports itself on every tracker command.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, on this repo, re-running this item's own scenario. With a\n10h-old marker and no owner, `tracker count-todos` prints:\n\n  [tracker] WARNING: ops self-healing has been OFF for 10h00m.\n    .git/tracker-recover-disabled is present with no auto-pr and no tracker\n    sync holding it -- the signature of a hard kill (SIGKILL / OOM; SIGTERM\n    and SIGINT both run the cleanup).\n    While it is there the reference-transaction and post-checkout hooks skip\n    `tracker recover`, so a `git reset --hard` or `git checkout` drops pending\n    .ops with nothing to restore them. The journal still holds the data --\n    this is degraded safety, not loss.\n    Clear it with:  rm -f .git/tracker-recover-disabled\n\nSame marker with `.git/PR_PENDING` beside it: silent. Marker absent: silent.\n\nTHE PREMISE WAS EXECUTED, NOT READ. Against a stub tracker in a throwaway repo,\nthe marker-ABSENT arm invokes `recover` and the marker-PRESENT arm invokes\nnothing, in BOTH hooks. The difference arm is what makes the silence mean\nsomething.\n\nTWO OF THIS ITEM'S OWN CLAIMS DID NOT SURVIVE THE CHECK.\n\n1. REFUTED -- the age discriminator. This item proposed warning above ~15\n   minutes \"because no auto-pr fetch+ff window is that long\". The marker is not\n   scoped to the fetch+ff. `do_pr` touches it as its FIRST act (auto-pr:1497)\n   and only `_autopr_finalize` removes it (auto-pr:380), so it spans the entire\n   run including the CI poll -- default timeout 2400s at\n   `scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh:623`, plus a 300s soft-retry at auto-pr:1935. A\n   15-minute rule fires INSIDE the legitimate window, on every run whose CI is\n   slow. So ownership is asked first and age only breaks the remaining tie.\n\n2. STALE -- the proposed surface. This item names `tracker recover`, since\n   deprecated in favour of `reconcile`, which was itself silent about the\n   marker while being the command AGENTS.md sends operators to for exactly this\n   class of repair. The warning is therefore wired at the single `main` exit,\n   so every subcommand carries it -- `recover`, `reconcile` and `count-todos`\n   included -- and it is not gated on exit code, because a `reconcile` that just\n   failed is when knowing self-healing is off changes what you do next.\n\nREFINEMENT TO THE LEAK STORY. Measured per-signal: bash runs the EXIT trap on\nSIGTERM and on SIGINT, and not on SIGKILL. The leak path is a hard kill and\nnothing else -- which is live here, not theoretical; the OOM reaper has killed\nauto-pr in this repo.\n\nAND THE REASON THE OBSERVED WINDOW WAS SILENT. `PR_PENDING` and the marker have\nDIFFERENT SPANS: `do_pr` removes `PR_PENDING` immediately after the merge\n(auto-pr:1432) but holds the marker until exit. This item's incident -- \"merged\n#635 successfully, then died during its post-merge local sync\" -- is exactly\nthat gap, where the loud gate has already been released and the silent one has\nnot. \"Marker present, no PR_PENDING\" is therefore not a heuristic; it is the\nsignature of the failure that was actually observed.\n\nTHE \"DO NOT AUTO-DELETE\" RULING IS HONOURED AND WAS RIGHT. Nothing here deletes\nthe marker. Ownership is read, never revoked.\n\nOPTIONAL HALF DELIBERATELY NOT FILED. This item offered a stop-hook nudge as an\noptional third check. Not filed, and the reason is written down rather than\ndropped silently: the warning now rides the stderr of every tracker command, and\nan agent runs those constantly, so the stop-hook surface would add a second\nchannel to the same reader. If a HUMAN-facing surface is wanted -- the TUI does\nnot show this -- that is a different item and worth filing on its own terms.\n\nRESIDUAL FILED: WI-gokuv -- give the marker a HOLDER instead of a flag (an fcntl\nlock, as WI-nutin already did for the sibling `TRACKER_SYNC_PENDING`), which\nremoves the window rather than reporting it. Governance-gated (scripts/auto-pr,\n.githooks/**), P3, needs_human_review."  # b26e
